    "q-2478": {
      "dom_id": "step-q2478",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ on the interval $[0,4].$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-0}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2})|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {4}^{3/2}-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{c} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ c & =\\frac{16}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-2478-a",
