    "q-120317": {
      "dom_id": "step-q120317",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+10$ on the interval $[-2,4].$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}2{x}^{2}+10\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+10x)|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{2\\cdot {4}^{3}}{3}+10\\cdot 4)-(\\frac{2\\cdot (-2)^{3}}{3}+10\\cdot (-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 108 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =18 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}+10 & =18 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =4 \\\\ c & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
