    "q-344694": {
      "dom_id": "step-q344694",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ on the interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0)}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3}{\\pi }(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
