    "q-120452": {
      "dom_id": "step-q120452",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x-10$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $8.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(3{x}^{2}-6x-10)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & ={\\frac{1}{c}({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-10x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 8 & =\\frac{1}{c}[({c}^{3}-3{c}^{2}-10c)-0] \\\\ 8 & ={c}^{2}-3c-10 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-3c-18 \\\\ 0 & =(c+3)(c-6) \\\\ c & =-3,\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $c>0,$ we conclude that $c=6$ only.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
