    "q-120721": {
      "dom_id": "step-q120721",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=9{x}^{2}+6x-18$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(9{x}^{2}+6x-18)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-18x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(3{c}^{3}+3{c}^{2}-18c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =3{c}^{2}+3c-18 \\\\ 0 & =(c+3)(3c-6) \\\\ c & =-3,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $c>0,$ we conclude that $c=2$ only.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
