    "q-344604": {
      "dom_id": "step-q344604",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=9\\sqrt{x}+2$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $11$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 11 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(9\\sqrt{x}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 11 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(6{x}^{3/2}+2x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 11 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(6{c}^{3/2}+2c)-0] \\\\ 11 & =6\\sqrt{c}+2 \\\\ 9 & =6\\sqrt{c} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & =\\sqrt{c} \\\\ c & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
