      "source_example_id": "e-549",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function",
      "kp_id": "e-549"
    },
    "q-316309": {
      "dom_id": "step-q316309",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14153257/assets/1c69b5a43e445861a728fcd8faed9e89b3bcb61141ad35d99e60f2a43983244d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-2,9],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(5,0)$ with radius $3.$ \n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[0,8].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,2].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,8].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8-0}\\cdot (-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
