      "source_example_id": "e-550",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph",
      "kp_id": "e-550"
    },
    "q-15237": {
      "dom_id": "step-q15237",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14153257/assets/97b55bafaa70ef2984575a30f06209e11304ff975df689833134fa672fdd7183.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-5,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$, $7$ and $3,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-5,4].$",
      "worked_solution": "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-5+7-3=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-5)}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
